// =============================================================================
// Chora Content Creation — Question authoring lifecycle events
// =============================================================================
//
// Source-of-truth: docs/m14/cr-question-authoring-design-2026-05-15.md §6
//   + ~/.claude/plans/golden-hopping-owl.md (D4 — async-everything)
//   + .claude/skills/pub-sub-topology
//
// Aggregate root : Question (sub-entity of LearningAtom — design §2.6)
// Owning domain  : Content Creation (chora_creation database)
// Owning team    : Team 1 (Content)
// Topic prefix   : chora.creation.question.*
// Surface (admin): A+ Creator mode
//
// Three topics defined here (topic format chora.{domain}.{aggregate}.{event}.v{N}
// per chora-contracts/CLAUDE.md §2):
//
//   - chora.creation.question.authored.v1
//       Fired on POST manual create + on accept of an AI-generated candidate
//       (both manual + accepted-AI paths create new Questions). Consumers:
//       chora-consumption (atom-cache invalidation, refresh learner projection
//       of mcq_payload / essay_payload), chora-sharing (atom-card update),
//       Observability + O+ (per-author authoring volume metric).
//
//   - chora.creation.question.generation_requested.v1
//       Fired by the chora-creation outbox at job creation time (D4 — every
//       AI call is async). The chora-creation question-generation worker
//       subscribes this topic, dispatches to Vertex AI Agent Engine
//       (qgen_per_question for single-question jobs OR qgen_batch +
//       chora-doc-parser for batch jobs), and on completion writes the
//       candidate_questions_jsonb + emits .generation_completed.v1.
//
//   - chora.creation.question.generation_completed.v1
//       Fired by the worker on terminal job status (success or failure).
//       Consumers: Observability + O+ (job latency + cost dashboards),
//       Notifications (notify author the job is ready for review or failed),
//       chora-governance (record per-job IMDA D1 accountability evidence).
//
// Every event embeds chora.common.v1.EventEnvelope as field 1 — tenant scope,
// GCID, trace context, schema version, and IMDA dimension tagging all live in
// the envelope per ddd-enforcement.md "Event envelope mandatory fields".
//
// Cross-DB queries FORBIDDEN — these events are the ONLY mechanism for
// cross-domain notification of question-authoring activity (per
// chora-contracts/CLAUDE.md §4).
